From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] home: keep the character that summons the search entry

Home implements Sugar's type-to-search: the first printable key moves focus
to the search entry. GTK has already chosen the event target by then, so the
character that triggered the move was never delivered and typing "Clock"
searched for "lock". Insert it directly and consume the event, which is what
GTK3 Sugar does.
--- a/src/jarabe/desktop/homewindow.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/desktop/homewindow.py
@@ -239,7 +239,13 @@
 
             if not has_focus:
                 search_entry.grab_focus()
-
+                # Focus moved mid-dispatch, so GTK will not deliver this key
+                # to the entry. The character that summoned search belongs in
+                # it, as it does in GTK3 Sugar.
+                search_entry.set_text(
+                    search_entry.get_text() + chr(unicode_char))
+                search_entry.set_position(-1)
+                return True
 
         return False
 
